    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# Task: implement multi-market listing publication and centralized market/category management for Shongre\n\nAnalyze the entire Shongre codebase and **implement or improve the complete multi-market architecture** so that, during publication, a seller can choose **one or several markets in which the same listing will be available**, while administrators centrally manage which countries/markets exist, which are enabled, and which categories, subcategories, attributes, services, and publication rules are available in each market.\n\nThe implementation must work with the current application, preserve existing behavior, avoid duplicate logic, use the existing design system and taxonomy, remain backend-ready, and make **France the default/primary market** while supporting future international expansion cleanly.\n\n## 1. Core business concept\n\nSeparate the following concepts clearly:\n\n* **Listing**: the canonical seller advertisement.\n* **Market**: a commercial/geographical market where Shongre operates.\n* **Country**: country associated with a market.\n* **Region/city/zone**: optional subdivisions of a market.\n* **Taxonomy**: global categories/subcategories/types/subtypes/attributes.\n* **Market taxonomy availability**: determines which taxonomy elements are usable in a given market.\n* **Listing market publication**: association between one listing and one or several markets.\n\nDo **not duplicate the listing** when the seller selects multiple markets.\n\nA single listing should conceptually behave like:\n\n```text\nListing\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Seller\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Canonical content\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Category / subtype\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Price\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Media\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Seller location\n \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Market publications\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 France\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: active\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 visibility rules\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Belgium\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: active\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 visibility rules\n      \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Switzerland\n           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: inactive\n```\n\nPrepare the frontend/domain layer for a backend model similar to:\n\n```ts\ntype Listing = {\n  id: string;\n  sellerId: string;\n\n  categoryId: string;\n  subcategoryId?: string;\n  subtypeId?: string;\n\n  title: string;\n  description: string;\n  price: Money;\n\n  location: ListingLocation;\n\n  marketPublications: ListingMarketPublication[];\n};\n\ntype ListingMarketPublication = {\n  marketId: string;\n  status:\n    | \"draft\"\n    | \"pending\"\n    | \"active\"\n    | \"paused\"\n    | \"rejected\"\n    | \"expired\";\n\n  publishedAt?: string;\n  expiresAt?: string;\n\n  localizedPrice?: Money;\n\n  visibility?: {\n    countryWide?: boolean;\n    regionIds?: string[];\n    cityIds?: string[];\n  };\n};\n```\n\nThe exact implementation should adapt to the current architecture instead of blindly creating parallel models.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Seller publication flow\n\nUpdate the complete publication flow so that a seller can select **multiple eligible markets**.\n\nCreate or improve a publication step such as:\n\n**O\303\271 souhaitez-vous publier cette annonce ?**\n\nDisplay the available markets as polished selectable cards/check rows, for example:\n\n```text\nMarch\303\251s de publication\n\n\342\230\221 France\n  March\303\251 principal \302\267 EUR\n\n\342\230\220 Belgique\n  EUR\n\n\342\230\220 Suisse\n  CHF\n\n\342\230\220 Luxembourg\n  EUR\n```\n\nDo not hardcode these countries in the component.\n\nThey must come from the centralized market configuration/data layer.\n\nSupport:\n\n* single selection;\n* multiple selection;\n* select all eligible markets when appropriate;\n* deselect;\n* disabled markets;\n* markets unavailable for the current category;\n* markets unavailable for the seller;\n* markets requiring additional information;\n* market-specific restrictions.\n\nFrance should automatically be selected as the default market when appropriate, while remaining editable if business rules allow it.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Context-aware market eligibility\n\nThe list shown to a seller must automatically depend on:\n\n```text\nseller\n+ seller type\n+ seller country\n+ listing category\n+ listing subtype\n+ market configuration\n+ publication permissions\n+ current market status\n```\n\nNever show an invalid selectable market and then fail silently later.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nV\303\251hicules\n\nFrance        \342\234\223 Disponible\nBelgique      \342\234\223 Disponible\nSuisse        \342\200\224 Non disponible pour cette cat\303\251gorie\n```\n\nUse a reusable domain selector/service such as:\n\n```ts\ngetEligibleMarketsForListing({\n  seller,\n  categoryId,\n  subtypeId,\n});\n```\n\nDo not scatter market eligibility conditions throughout components.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Category availability per market\n\nAdmin must be able to control which taxonomy branches are available in every market.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrance\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 V\303\251hicules \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Immobilier \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Emploi \342\234\223\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Services \342\234\223\n\nBelgique\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 V\303\251hicules \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Immobilier \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Emploi \342\234\225\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Services \342\234\223\n```\n\nSupport configuration at the appropriate levels:\n\n```text\ncategory\n  \342\206\222 subcategory\n      \342\206\222 type\n          \342\206\222 subtype\n              \342\206\222 attributes\n```\n\nPrefer inheritance.\n\nFor example, enabling a category can enable all children by default unless explicitly overridden.\n\nDo not clone the complete taxonomy for every country.\n\nKeep:\n\n```text\nGLOBAL TAXONOMY\n        \342\206\223\nMARKET AVAILABILITY / OVERRIDES\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Market-specific taxonomy configuration\n\nPrepare the architecture to eventually support market-specific variations such as:\n\n* category enabled/disabled;\n* subcategory enabled/disabled;\n* attribute enabled/disabled;\n* required/optional attribute differences;\n* allowed attribute values;\n* labels/translations;\n* legal requirements;\n* publication limits;\n* price constraints;\n* professional-only categories;\n* individual-only categories.\n\nFor example:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketTaxonomyRule = {\n  marketId: string;\n  taxonomyNodeId: string;\n\n  enabled: boolean;\n\n  required?: boolean;\n\n  allowedValues?: string[];\n\n  sellerTypes?: Array<\"individual\" | \"professional\">;\n};\n```\n\nReuse the current Shongre taxonomy architecture and avoid unnecessary migration if equivalent concepts already exist.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Dynamic publication form\n\nThe publication form must react immediately to selected markets.\n\nIf all selected markets use the same fields:\n\n\342\206\222 show the normal form once.\n\nIf a selected market introduces additional mandatory fields:\n\n\342\206\222 display those additional requirements clearly.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nInformations compl\303\251mentaires\n\nRequises pour publier en Suisse\n\n\342\200\242 Type d\'immatriculation\n\342\200\242 Canton\n```\n\nDo not duplicate the full form for every selected country.\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nglobal/common fields\n+\nmarket-specific requirements\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. Validation\n\nBefore allowing publication, validate the listing against **every selected market**.\n\nCreate centralized validation similar to:\n\n```ts\nvalidateListingForMarkets({\n  listing,\n  marketIds,\n});\n```\n\nReturn structured results:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketValidationResult = {\n  marketId: string;\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationIssue[];\n  warnings: ValidationIssue[];\n};\n```\n\nExample UI:\n\n```text\nValidation des march\303\251s\n\n\342\234\223 France\n  Pr\303\252te \303\240 \303\252tre publi\303\251e\n\n\342\234\223 Belgique\n  Pr\303\252te \303\240 \303\252tre publi\303\251e\n\n! Suisse\n  2 informations manquantes\n```\n\nThe seller should be able to understand exactly which market requires a correction.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Publication confirmation\n\nBefore final submission, display a concise summary:\n\n```text\nVotre annonce sera publi\303\251e dans 3 march\303\251s\n\n\360\237\207\253\360\237\207\267 France\n\360\237\207\247\360\237\207\252 Belgique\n\360\237\207\250\360\237\207\255 Suisse\n```\n\nAlso summarize when relevant:\n\n* currency;\n* publication price;\n* boosts;\n* optional paid services;\n* restrictions;\n* estimated publication duration.\n\nUse the existing monetization system rather than creating separate pricing logic.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Market-specific monetization\n\nPrepare the architecture so publication pricing and monetization can differ by market.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nFrance\nPublication gratuite\n\nBelgique\nPublication gratuite\n\nSuisse\n3,00 CHF\n```\n\nAdmin should eventually be able to configure:\n\n* free publication;\n* paid publication;\n* listing limits;\n* boosts;\n* featured listings;\n* urgent badge;\n* store plans;\n* professional subscriptions;\n* commission;\n* payment fees;\n* delivery fees.\n\nReuse Shongre\'s centralized monetization system.\n\nDo not hardcode monetary rules inside the publication form.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Listing management after publication\n\nIn the seller workspace, show where each listing is currently published.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nMacBook Pro M4\n\nActive dans 3 march\303\251s\n\nFrance       Active\nBelgique     Active\nSuisse       Active\n```\n\nProvide actions such as:\n\n```text\nG\303\251rer les march\303\251s\n```\n\nThe seller should be able to:\n\n* add another eligible market;\n* remove a market;\n* pause publication in one market;\n* reactivate it;\n* inspect rejection/restriction reasons.\n\nDo not require the seller to recreate the listing.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Market-specific status\n\nSupport per-market lifecycle states.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrance       Active\nBelgique     En validation\nSuisse       Refus\303\251e\n```\n\nThe overall listing may still remain active as long as one market publication is active.\n\nNever model the whole listing as rejected because one market rejected it.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Admin: centralized Market Management\n\nImplement or improve a dedicated administration area such as:\n\n```text\nAdmin\n  \342\206\222 Configuration\n      \342\206\222 March\303\251s\n```\n\nor reuse the existing admin information architecture if a market-management section already exists.\n\nThe admin market overview should show:\n\n| March\303\251   | Pays | Devise | Langue   | Statut    | Cat\303\251gories | Annonces |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | --------- | ---------- | -------- |\n| France   | FR   | EUR    | fr       | Actif     | 22         | ...      |\n| Belgique | BE   | EUR    | fr/nl    | Actif     | 18         | ...      |\n| Suisse   | CH   | CHF    | fr/de/it | Brouillon | 12         | ...      |\n\nProvide appropriate actions:\n\n* create market;\n* edit;\n* enable;\n* disable;\n* archive;\n* duplicate configuration;\n* configure taxonomy;\n* configure geographic scope;\n* configure seller eligibility;\n* configure publication rules.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Admin market configuration\n\nEach market should have configuration sections such as:\n\n### General\n\n* internal ID;\n* name;\n* short label;\n* country;\n* country ISO code;\n* currency;\n* default locale;\n* supported locales;\n* timezone;\n* phone prefix;\n* market status;\n* launch date;\n* default market indicator.\n\n### Geographic coverage\n\nSupport:\n\n```text\nToute la France\n```\n\nor specific:\n\n```text\nRegions\nDepartments\nCities\nPostal codes\n```\n\nPrepare the architecture for countries that use different administrative divisions.\n\nDo not make the domain model France-specific.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Market status\n\nSupport at least:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketStatus =\n  | \"draft\"\n  | \"scheduled\"\n  | \"active\"\n  | \"paused\"\n  | \"disabled\"\n  | \"archived\";\n```\n\nA market not active must never appear as a publication target for regular sellers.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Admin category management per market\n\nInside each market provide:\n\n```text\nCat\303\251gories disponibles\n```\n\nwith:\n\n* search;\n* hierarchical tree;\n* expand/collapse;\n* bulk enable;\n* bulk disable;\n* inheritance indicators;\n* overrides;\n* seller-type restrictions.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n\342\230\221 V\303\251hicules\n   \342\230\221 Voitures\n   \342\230\221 Motos\n   \342\230\220 Nautisme\n\n\342\230\221 Immobilier\n\n\342\230\220 Emploi\n```\n\nChanges must use the same taxonomy consumed by:\n\n* publication;\n* search;\n* filters;\n* listing details;\n* seller workspace;\n* homepage/category navigation.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Prevent invalid existing listings\n\nAdmin changes must not silently corrupt existing listings.\n\nFor example, if an admin disables:\n\n```text\nBelgique \342\206\222 V\303\251hicules\n```\n\nand listings are already active there, require an explicit strategy.\n\nPossible admin warning:\n\n```text\nCette modification affectera 1 247 annonces actuellement publi\303\251es.\n```\n\nPossible operations:\n\n* affect new listings only;\n* stop new publications;\n* schedule deactivation;\n* deactivate existing listings.\n\nPrepare frontend contracts for these behaviors.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Market selector throughout Shongre\n\nEnsure the platform has a consistent concept of:\n\n```text\nactive browsing market\n```\n\nThis is different from:\n\n```text\nmarkets selected for a seller listing\n```\n\nDo not conflate them.\n\nFor example:\n\n```ts\nBrowsingMarketContext\n\nListingPublicationMarkets\n```\n\nThe user\'s currently viewed market should affect:\n\n* search results;\n* category availability;\n* homepage;\n* filters;\n* pricing;\n* currency;\n* localization;\n* recommendations.\n\n---\n\n# 18. Search behavior\n\nA listing associated with multiple markets must be discoverable in each eligible market.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nListing #123\nmarkets = [FR, BE]\n```\n\nSearching France:\n\n\342\206\222 appears.\n\nSearching Belgium:\n\n\342\206\222 appears.\n\nSearching Switzerland:\n\n\342\206\222 does not appear.\n\nPrepare query contracts such as:\n\n```text\n/recherche?market=fr\n```\n\nor the architecture already used by the application.\n\nAvoid encoding important market state only inside presentation components.\n\n---\n\n# 19. URL strategy\n\nReview the current routing architecture and prepare it for country-aware URLs.\n\nPossible long-term structure:\n\n```text\n/fr/...\n/be/...\n/ch/...\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\n?market=fr\n```\n\nChoose a strategy compatible with the existing architecture.\n\nDo not perform an unnecessary breaking URL migration unless required.\n\nDocument the decision.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Currency\n\nEach market must define its default currency.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nFrance \342\206\222 EUR\nBelgium \342\206\222 EUR\nSwitzerland \342\206\222 CHF\nUnited Kingdom \342\206\222 GBP\n```\n\nPrepare for:\n\n* canonical listing price;\n* optional market-localized price;\n* currency display;\n* conversion strategy;\n* pricing overrides.\n\nDo not perform automatic currency conversions using fake rates in demo mode.\n\nUse deterministic mock rates only if the current frontend specifically needs to demonstrate the capability, and clearly identify them as demo data.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Language and localization\n\nMarket and language must remain separate concepts.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nBelgium\n  \342\206\222 French\n  \342\206\222 Dutch\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\nSwitzerland\n  \342\206\222 French\n  \342\206\222 German\n  \342\206\222 Italian\n```\n\nDo not assume:\n\n```text\n1 market = 1 language\n```\n\nPrepare the model accordingly.\n\n---\n\n# 22. Seller permissions\n\nThe publication markets available may eventually depend on:\n\n* account country;\n* individual/professional status;\n* verified identity;\n* KYC;\n* business verification;\n* professional subscription;\n* billing address;\n* VAT configuration;\n* category;\n* legal restrictions.\n\nCentralize these rules.\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\ncanSellerPublishInMarket({\n  seller,\n  market,\n  listing,\n});\n```\n\nDo not embed large permission expressions in React JSX.\n\n---\n\n# 23. Seller UX\n\nThe seller experience must remain simple even though the underlying model is powerful.\n\nPreferred publication UX:\n\n```text\n1. Cat\303\251gorie\n2. Description\n3. Photos\n4. Prix\n5. Livraison\n6. March\303\251s\n7. V\303\251rification\n8. Publication\n```\n\nAdapt this order to the current Shongre publication journey if necessary.\n\nDo not make the seller configure technical concepts such as currencies, locales or taxonomy IDs directly.\n\n---\n\n# 24. Professional sellers\n\nEnsure the feature works for both:\n\n```text\nParticulier\nProfessionnel\n```\n\nProfessional sellers may eventually need additional tools:\n\n* default publication markets;\n* bulk market assignment;\n* store markets;\n* catalog-wide markets;\n* market-specific inventory;\n* market-specific subscriptions.\n\nPrepare the architecture for these without overcomplicating the first implementation.\n\n---\n\n# 25. Default seller preferences\n\nAdd support for seller publication preferences such as:\n\n```ts\ndefaultPublicationMarketIds: string[];\n```\n\nFor example, a professional seller may choose:\n\n```text\nPublier par d\303\251faut dans :\n\342\234\223 France\n\342\234\223 Belgique\n```\n\nPublication should initialize from these preferences but allow editing when permitted.\n\n---\n\n# 26. Admin global market controls\n\nAdmin should be able to define:\n\n```text\nPlatform default market: France\n```\n\nand possibly:\n\n```text\nFallback market: France\n```\n\nNever hardcode `FR` throughout the application.\n\nExpose selectors/helpers such as:\n\n```ts\ngetDefaultMarket()\ngetActiveMarkets()\ngetMarketById()\ngetMarketsForCategory()\n```\n\n---\n\n# 27. Demo mode\n\nBecause Shongre currently has frontend/demo capabilities, implement deterministic fixtures demonstrating at least:\n\n### Markets\n\n```text\nFrance\nBelgique\nSuisse\nLuxembourg\n```\n\n### States\n\n* active market;\n* disabled market;\n* draft market;\n* category unavailable in market;\n* seller eligible in several markets;\n* seller eligible in one market only;\n* listing active in several markets;\n* listing with mixed per-market statuses.\n\nDo not create fake asynchronous APIs pretending a backend exists.\n\nUse the existing mock/demo data architecture.\n\n---\n\n# 28. Architecture\n\nAnalyze existing files first.\n\nDo not create another parallel market system if one already exists.\n\nPrefer a structure conceptually similar to:\n\n```text\nfrontend/\n  src/\n    domain/\n      markets/\n        types.ts\n        selectors.ts\n        permissions.ts\n        validation.ts\n\n    features/\n      markets/\n      publish/\n      admin/\n      search/\n\n    data/\n      markets/\n      marketTaxonomy/\n\n    components/\n      market/\n```\n\nAdapt names to the actual architecture.\n\nKeep:\n\n```text\nUI\n \342\206\223\nfeature/application layer\n \342\206\223\ndomain selectors/services\n \342\206\223\nrepository/data contracts\n```\n\nDo not let pages directly manipulate raw fixtures.\n\n---\n\n# 29. Backend-ready contracts\n\nAlthough this phase may primarily concern frontend implementation, ensure all models and operations can later map cleanly to APIs.\n\nPrepare repository interfaces/contracts such as:\n\n```ts\ninterface MarketRepository {\n  list(): Promise<Market[]>;\n  get(id: string): Promise<Market>;\n}\n\ninterface ListingMarketRepository {\n  getEligibleMarkets(input: EligibleMarketsInput): Promise<Market[]>;\n}\n```\n\nand eventual endpoints conceptually similar to:\n\n```text\nGET    /markets\nGET    /markets/:id\nGET    /markets/:id/taxonomy\n\nGET    /listings/:id/markets\n\nPOST   /listings/:id/markets\nPATCH  /listings/:id/markets/:marketId\nDELETE /listings/:id/markets/:marketId\n```\n\nFor admin:\n\n```text\nGET    /admin/markets\nPOST   /admin/markets\nPATCH  /admin/markets/:id\n\nGET    /admin/markets/:id/taxonomy\nPATCH  /admin/markets/:id/taxonomy\n```\n\nDo not implement fake network calls if no backend exists yet.\n\n---\n\n# 30. Search and indexing readiness\n\nEnsure the future search/indexing model can distinguish:\n\n```text\nlisting\n+\nmarket\n+\nmarket publication status\n```\n\nAn inactive market association must never make a listing visible in that market.\n\nA useful future indexing representation may resemble:\n\n```ts\n{\n  listingId: \"listing_123\",\n  activeMarketIds: [\"fr\", \"be\"],\n}\n```\n\nor one search document per `(listing, market)` if the search architecture eventually requires different localized data.\n\nKeep the current implementation flexible enough to support either.\n\n---\n\n# 31. Performance\n\nAvoid:\n\n* loading the entire global taxonomy repeatedly;\n* deep client-side scans on every render;\n* duplicating taxonomy trees per market;\n* expensive eligibility computations in JSX;\n* excessive localStorage access;\n* duplicate state between contexts/stores.\n\nUse:\n\n* normalized maps;\n* selectors;\n* memoization where useful;\n* existing state-management patterns.\n\n---\n\n# 32. Accessibility\n\nEnsure all multi-select controls are accessible.\n\nMarket selection must support:\n\n* keyboard navigation;\n* visible focus;\n* correct checkbox semantics;\n* screen-reader labels;\n* disabled-state explanation;\n* validation announcements;\n* no flag-only labels.\n\nNever rely solely on color or flags.\n\n---\n\n# 33. Responsive design\n\nEnsure the complete experience works on:\n\n* desktop web;\n* tablet;\n* mobile web;\n* iOS app/webview;\n* Android app/webview.\n\nOn mobile, market cards should become compact full-width rows.\n\nDo not allow horizontal overflow.\n\nAvoid oversized:\n\n* cards;\n* selectors;\n* modals;\n* text;\n* buttons;\n* spacing.\n\nUse existing responsive design tokens.\n\n---\n\n# 34. Design system\n\nUse existing Shongre primitives and tokens.\n\nDo not introduce:\n\n* hardcoded colors;\n* arbitrary radii;\n* duplicate buttons;\n* duplicate badges;\n* duplicate modal systems;\n* isolated spacing systems.\n\nReuse existing:\n\n* Button;\n* Badge;\n* FormField;\n* Modal/Drawer;\n* StatePanel;\n* Notice;\n* Checkbox;\n* SectionHeader;\n* admin table/list primitives;\n\nor their actual equivalents in the repository.\n\n---\n\n# 35. Admin UX quality\n\nAdmin market management should feel like a professional SaaS back office.\n\nUse:\n\n* clear information hierarchy;\n* compact controls;\n* search;\n* filters;\n* badges;\n* bulk actions;\n* confirmation dialogs;\n* impact previews;\n* empty states;\n* error states;\n* skeleton/loading states;\n* unsaved-changes indication where relevant.\n\nAvoid giant cards or unnecessarily large controls.\n\n---\n\n# 36. Market removal safety\n\nMarkets referenced by listings must not be physically deleted casually.\n\nPrefer:\n\n```text\ndisable\narchive\n```\n\ninstead of hard deletion.\n\nIf hard deletion exists, make it an exceptional protected operation.\n\n---\n\n# 37. Audit existing functionality\n\nBefore implementation, inspect all affected areas, including:\n\n```text\npublication flow\nlisting creation state\nlisting editing\nlisting management\nseller workspace\nseller store\nsearch\nresults\nhomepage\ntaxonomy\nfilters\nadmin\nmarket management\nmonetization\nauthentication\nseller roles\nlocalization\ncurrency\nrouting\ndemo fixtures\n```\n\nFind duplicated or inconsistent country/market concepts and consolidate them.\n\n---\n\n# 38. Migration and backward compatibility\n\nExisting listings that have no explicit market assignment must continue to work.\n\nIntroduce a migration/fallback rule such as:\n\n```text\nlegacy listing without market\n\342\206\222 default market = France\n```\n\nDo this in one centralized compatibility layer.\n\nDo not sprinkle:\n\n```ts\nmarketId ?? \"fr\"\n```\n\nthroughout the codebase.\n\n---\n\n# 39. Tests\n\nAdd/update tests covering at minimum:\n\n### Publication\n\n* France selected by default;\n* seller selects multiple markets;\n* seller deselects market;\n* disabled market cannot be selected;\n* unavailable category prevents selection;\n* market-specific validation;\n* successful multi-market publication.\n\n### Admin\n\n* create market;\n* enable/disable market;\n* configure category availability;\n* inherited taxonomy state;\n* override taxonomy state;\n* market disabled disappears from seller publication choices.\n\n### Listings\n\n* one listing available in several markets;\n* per-market status;\n* remove a market without deleting listing;\n* legacy listings resolve to France.\n\n### Search\n\n* listing appears only in active associated markets.\n\n### Roles\n\nTest at least:\n\n```text\nvisitor\nindividual seller\nprofessional seller\nadmin\nmoderator where relevant\n```\n\n---\n\n# 40. Acceptance criteria\n\nThe work is complete only when:\n\n* a seller can select **more than one market** during publication;\n* the listing remains one canonical listing;\n* each selected market has its own publication association/status;\n* France remains the default market;\n* markets come from centralized configuration;\n* admin can create/configure/enable/disable markets;\n* admin can associate categories with each market;\n* taxonomy is not unnecessarily duplicated;\n* publication options dynamically respect category/market compatibility;\n* seller receives clear feedback about unavailable markets;\n* market-specific validation works;\n* existing listings remain compatible;\n* seller workspace shows all markets for each listing;\n* seller can manage market availability after publication;\n* search visibility respects market assignment;\n* individual and professional sellers are supported;\n* demo mode contains realistic deterministic examples;\n* UI is polished, compact, responsive and accessible;\n* design tokens/primitives are respected;\n* no fake backend behavior is introduced;\n* domain contracts are ready for the future backend;\n* tests pass;\n* lint/typecheck/build pass.\n\n---\n\n# 41. Final verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n\n1. inspect every modified flow visually;\n2. test desktop, tablet and mobile;\n3. test Particulier publication;\n4. test Professionnel publication;\n5. test listing associated with one market;\n6. test listing associated with several markets;\n7. disable a category for one market and verify publication reacts immediately;\n8. disable an entire market and verify it disappears from eligible publication choices;\n9. verify an existing active listing is not accidentally deleted;\n10. verify search is market-aware;\n11. verify France remains the safe default for legacy data;\n12. run tests;\n13. run lint;\n14. run TypeScript checks;\n15. run production build;\n16. remove obsolete/duplicated implementation discovered during the migration.\n\nFinally, update `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or the appropriate architecture documentation with the resulting rules, especially the distinction between:\n\n```text\ncountry\nmarket\nbrowsing market\nlisting publication markets\ntaxonomy\nmarket taxonomy availability\n```\n\nThe resulting architecture must make adding a new country/market mostly a **configuration operation rather than a frontend code change**, while keeping the publication experience extremely simple for sellers."
    items {
      text: "# Task: implement multi-market listing publication and centralized market/category management for Shongre\n\nAnalyze the entire Shongre codebase and **implement or improve the complete multi-market architecture** so that, during publication, a seller can choose **one or several markets in which the same listing will be available**, while administrators centrally manage which countries/markets exist, which are enabled, and which categories, subcategories, attributes, services, and publication rules are available in each market.\n\nThe implementation must work with the current application, preserve existing behavior, avoid duplicate logic, use the existing design system and taxonomy, remain backend-ready, and make **France the default/primary market** while supporting future international expansion cleanly.\n\n## 1. Core business concept\n\nSeparate the following concepts clearly:\n\n* **Listing**: the canonical seller advertisement.\n* **Market**: a commercial/geographical market where Shongre operates.\n* **Country**: country associated with a market.\n* **Region/city/zone**: optional subdivisions of a market.\n* **Taxonomy**: global categories/subcategories/types/subtypes/attributes.\n* **Market taxonomy availability**: determines which taxonomy elements are usable in a given market.\n* **Listing market publication**: association between one listing and one or several markets.\n\nDo **not duplicate the listing** when the seller selects multiple markets.\n\nA single listing should conceptually behave like:\n\n```text\nListing\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Seller\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Canonical content\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Category / subtype\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Price\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Media\n \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Seller location\n \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Market publications\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 France\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: active\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 visibility rules\n      \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Belgium\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: active\n      \342\224\202    \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 visibility rules\n      \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Switzerland\n           \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 status: inactive\n```\n\nPrepare the frontend/domain layer for a backend model similar to:\n\n```ts\ntype Listing = {\n  id: string;\n  sellerId: string;\n\n  categoryId: string;\n  subcategoryId?: string;\n  subtypeId?: string;\n\n  title: string;\n  description: string;\n  price: Money;\n\n  location: ListingLocation;\n\n  marketPublications: ListingMarketPublication[];\n};\n\ntype ListingMarketPublication = {\n  marketId: string;\n  status:\n    | \"draft\"\n    | \"pending\"\n    | \"active\"\n    | \"paused\"\n    | \"rejected\"\n    | \"expired\";\n\n  publishedAt?: string;\n  expiresAt?: string;\n\n  localizedPrice?: Money;\n\n  visibility?: {\n    countryWide?: boolean;\n    regionIds?: string[];\n    cityIds?: string[];\n  };\n};\n```\n\nThe exact implementation should adapt to the current architecture instead of blindly creating parallel models.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Seller publication flow\n\nUpdate the complete publication flow so that a seller can select **multiple eligible markets**.\n\nCreate or improve a publication step such as:\n\n**O\303\271 souhaitez-vous publier cette annonce ?**\n\nDisplay the available markets as polished selectable cards/check rows, for example:\n\n```text\nMarch\303\251s de publication\n\n\342\230\221 France\n  March\303\251 principal \302\267 EUR\n\n\342\230\220 Belgique\n  EUR\n\n\342\230\220 Suisse\n  CHF\n\n\342\230\220 Luxembourg\n  EUR\n```\n\nDo not hardcode these countries in the component.\n\nThey must come from the centralized market configuration/data layer.\n\nSupport:\n\n* single selection;\n* multiple selection;\n* select all eligible markets when appropriate;\n* deselect;\n* disabled markets;\n* markets unavailable for the current category;\n* markets unavailable for the seller;\n* markets requiring additional information;\n* market-specific restrictions.\n\nFrance should automatically be selected as the default market when appropriate, while remaining editable if business rules allow it.\n\n---\n\n# 3. Context-aware market eligibility\n\nThe list shown to a seller must automatically depend on:\n\n```text\nseller\n+ seller type\n+ seller country\n+ listing category\n+ listing subtype\n+ market configuration\n+ publication permissions\n+ current market status\n```\n\nNever show an invalid selectable market and then fail silently later.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nV\303\251hicules\n\nFrance        \342\234\223 Disponible\nBelgique      \342\234\223 Disponible\nSuisse        \342\200\224 Non disponible pour cette cat\303\251gorie\n```\n\nUse a reusable domain selector/service such as:\n\n```ts\ngetEligibleMarketsForListing({\n  seller,\n  categoryId,\n  subtypeId,\n});\n```\n\nDo not scatter market eligibility conditions throughout components.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Category availability per market\n\nAdmin must be able to control which taxonomy branches are available in every market.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrance\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 V\303\251hicules \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Immobilier \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Emploi \342\234\223\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Services \342\234\223\n\nBelgique\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 V\303\251hicules \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Immobilier \342\234\223\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Emploi \342\234\225\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Services \342\234\223\n```\n\nSupport configuration at the appropriate levels:\n\n```text\ncategory\n  \342\206\222 subcategory\n      \342\206\222 type\n          \342\206\222 subtype\n              \342\206\222 attributes\n```\n\nPrefer inheritance.\n\nFor example, enabling a category can enable all children by default unless explicitly overridden.\n\nDo not clone the complete taxonomy for every country.\n\nKeep:\n\n```text\nGLOBAL TAXONOMY\n        \342\206\223\nMARKET AVAILABILITY / OVERRIDES\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Market-specific taxonomy configuration\n\nPrepare the architecture to eventually support market-specific variations such as:\n\n* category enabled/disabled;\n* subcategory enabled/disabled;\n* attribute enabled/disabled;\n* required/optional attribute differences;\n* allowed attribute values;\n* labels/translations;\n* legal requirements;\n* publication limits;\n* price constraints;\n* professional-only categories;\n* individual-only categories.\n\nFor example:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketTaxonomyRule = {\n  marketId: string;\n  taxonomyNodeId: string;\n\n  enabled: boolean;\n\n  required?: boolean;\n\n  allowedValues?: string[];\n\n  sellerTypes?: Array<\"individual\" | \"professional\">;\n};\n```\n\nReuse the current Shongre taxonomy architecture and avoid unnecessary migration if equivalent concepts already exist.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Dynamic publication form\n\nThe publication form must react immediately to selected markets.\n\nIf all selected markets use the same fields:\n\n\342\206\222 show the normal form once.\n\nIf a selected market introduces additional mandatory fields:\n\n\342\206\222 display those additional requirements clearly.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nInformations compl\303\251mentaires\n\nRequises pour publier en Suisse\n\n\342\200\242 Type d\'immatriculation\n\342\200\242 Canton\n```\n\nDo not duplicate the full form for every selected country.\n\nBuild:\n\n```text\nglobal/common fields\n+\nmarket-specific requirements\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. Validation\n\nBefore allowing publication, validate the listing against **every selected market**.\n\nCreate centralized validation similar to:\n\n```ts\nvalidateListingForMarkets({\n  listing,\n  marketIds,\n});\n```\n\nReturn structured results:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketValidationResult = {\n  marketId: string;\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: ValidationIssue[];\n  warnings: ValidationIssue[];\n};\n```\n\nExample UI:\n\n```text\nValidation des march\303\251s\n\n\342\234\223 France\n  Pr\303\252te \303\240 \303\252tre publi\303\251e\n\n\342\234\223 Belgique\n  Pr\303\252te \303\240 \303\252tre publi\303\251e\n\n! Suisse\n  2 informations manquantes\n```\n\nThe seller should be able to understand exactly which market requires a correction.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Publication confirmation\n\nBefore final submission, display a concise summary:\n\n```text\nVotre annonce sera publi\303\251e dans 3 march\303\251s\n\n\360\237\207\253\360\237\207\267 France\n\360\237\207\247\360\237\207\252 Belgique\n\360\237\207\250\360\237\207\255 Suisse\n```\n\nAlso summarize when relevant:\n\n* currency;\n* publication price;\n* boosts;\n* optional paid services;\n* restrictions;\n* estimated publication duration.\n\nUse the existing monetization system rather than creating separate pricing logic.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Market-specific monetization\n\nPrepare the architecture so publication pricing and monetization can differ by market.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nFrance\nPublication gratuite\n\nBelgique\nPublication gratuite\n\nSuisse\n3,00 CHF\n```\n\nAdmin should eventually be able to configure:\n\n* free publication;\n* paid publication;\n* listing limits;\n* boosts;\n* featured listings;\n* urgent badge;\n* store plans;\n* professional subscriptions;\n* commission;\n* payment fees;\n* delivery fees.\n\nReuse Shongre\'s centralized monetization system.\n\nDo not hardcode monetary rules inside the publication form.\n\n---\n\n# 10. Listing management after publication\n\nIn the seller workspace, show where each listing is currently published.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nMacBook Pro M4\n\nActive dans 3 march\303\251s\n\nFrance       Active\nBelgique     Active\nSuisse       Active\n```\n\nProvide actions such as:\n\n```text\nG\303\251rer les march\303\251s\n```\n\nThe seller should be able to:\n\n* add another eligible market;\n* remove a market;\n* pause publication in one market;\n* reactivate it;\n* inspect rejection/restriction reasons.\n\nDo not require the seller to recreate the listing.\n\n---\n\n# 11. Market-specific status\n\nSupport per-market lifecycle states.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nFrance       Active\nBelgique     En validation\nSuisse       Refus\303\251e\n```\n\nThe overall listing may still remain active as long as one market publication is active.\n\nNever model the whole listing as rejected because one market rejected it.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Admin: centralized Market Management\n\nImplement or improve a dedicated administration area such as:\n\n```text\nAdmin\n  \342\206\222 Configuration\n      \342\206\222 March\303\251s\n```\n\nor reuse the existing admin information architecture if a market-management section already exists.\n\nThe admin market overview should show:\n\n| March\303\251   | Pays | Devise | Langue   | Statut    | Cat\303\251gories | Annonces |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | --------- | ---------- | -------- |\n| France   | FR   | EUR    | fr       | Actif     | 22         | ...      |\n| Belgique | BE   | EUR    | fr/nl    | Actif     | 18         | ...      |\n| Suisse   | CH   | CHF    | fr/de/it | Brouillon | 12         | ...      |\n\nProvide appropriate actions:\n\n* create market;\n* edit;\n* enable;\n* disable;\n* archive;\n* duplicate configuration;\n* configure taxonomy;\n* configure geographic scope;\n* configure seller eligibility;\n* configure publication rules.\n\n---\n\n# 13. Admin market configuration\n\nEach market should have configuration sections such as:\n\n### General\n\n* internal ID;\n* name;\n* short label;\n* country;\n* country ISO code;\n* currency;\n* default locale;\n* supported locales;\n* timezone;\n* phone prefix;\n* market status;\n* launch date;\n* default market indicator.\n\n### Geographic coverage\n\nSupport:\n\n```text\nToute la France\n```\n\nor specific:\n\n```text\nRegions\nDepartments\nCities\nPostal codes\n```\n\nPrepare the architecture for countries that use different administrative divisions.\n\nDo not make the domain model France-specific.\n\n---\n\n# 14. Market status\n\nSupport at least:\n\n```ts\ntype MarketStatus =\n  | \"draft\"\n  | \"scheduled\"\n  | \"active\"\n  | \"paused\"\n  | \"disabled\"\n  | \"archived\";\n```\n\nA market not active must never appear as a publication target for regular sellers.\n\n---\n\n# 15. Admin category management per market\n\nInside each market provide:\n\n```text\nCat\303\251gories disponibles\n```\n\nwith:\n\n* search;\n* hierarchical tree;\n* expand/collapse;\n* bulk enable;\n* bulk disable;\n* inheritance indicators;\n* overrides;\n* seller-type restrictions.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\n\342\230\221 V\303\251hicules\n   \342\230\221 Voitures\n   \342\230\221 Motos\n   \342\230\220 Nautisme\n\n\342\230\221 Immobilier\n\n\342\230\220 Emploi\n```\n\nChanges must use the same taxonomy consumed by:\n\n* publication;\n* search;\n* filters;\n* listing details;\n* seller workspace;\n* homepage/category navigation.\n\n---\n\n# 16. Prevent invalid existing listings\n\nAdmin changes must not silently corrupt existing listings.\n\nFor example, if an admin disables:\n\n```text\nBelgique \342\206\222 V\303\251hicules\n```\n\nand listings are already active there, require an explicit strategy.\n\nPossible admin warning:\n\n```text\nCette modification affectera 1 247 annonces actuellement publi\303\251es.\n```\n\nPossible operations:\n\n* affect new listings only;\n* stop new publications;\n* schedule deactivation;\n* deactivate existing listings.\n\nPrepare frontend contracts for these behaviors.\n\n---\n\n# 17. Market selector throughout Shongre\n\nEnsure the platform has a consistent concept of:\n\n```text\nactive browsing market\n```\n\nThis is different from:\n\n```text\nmarkets selected for a seller listing\n```\n\nDo not conflate them.\n\nFor example:\n\n```ts\nBrowsingMarketContext\n\nListingPublicationMarkets\n```\n\nThe user\'s currently viewed market should affect:\n\n* search results;\n* category availability;\n* homepage;\n* filters;\n* pricing;\n* currency;\n* localization;\n* recommendations.\n\n---\n\n# 18. Search behavior\n\nA listing associated with multiple markets must be discoverable in each eligible market.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nListing #123\nmarkets = [FR, BE]\n```\n\nSearching France:\n\n\342\206\222 appears.\n\nSearching Belgium:\n\n\342\206\222 appears.\n\nSearching Switzerland:\n\n\342\206\222 does not appear.\n\nPrepare query contracts such as:\n\n```text\n/recherche?market=fr\n```\n\nor the architecture already used by the application.\n\nAvoid encoding important market state only inside presentation components.\n\n---\n\n# 19. URL strategy\n\nReview the current routing architecture and prepare it for country-aware URLs.\n\nPossible long-term structure:\n\n```text\n/fr/...\n/be/...\n/ch/...\n```\n\nor:\n\n```text\n?market=fr\n```\n\nChoose a strategy compatible with the existing architecture.\n\nDo not perform an unnecessary breaking URL migration unless required.\n\nDocument the decision.\n\n---\n\n# 20. Currency\n\nEach market must define its default currency.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nFrance \342\206\222 EUR\nBelgium \342\206\222 EUR\nSwitzerland \342\206\222 CHF\nUnited Kingdom \342\206\222 GBP\n```\n\nPrepare for:\n\n* canonical listing price;\n* optional market-localized price;\n* currency display;\n* conversion strategy;\n* pricing overrides.\n\nDo not perform automatic currency conversions using fake rates in demo mode.\n\nUse deterministic mock rates only if the current frontend specifically needs to demonstrate the capability, and clearly identify them as demo data.\n\n---\n\n# 21. Language and localization\n\nMarket and language must remain separate concepts.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nBelgium\n  \342\206\222 French\n  \342\206\222 Dutch\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\nSwitzerland\n  \342\206\222 French\n  \342\206\222 German\n  \342\206\222 Italian\n```\n\nDo not assume:\n\n```text\n1 market = 1 language\n```\n\nPrepare the model accordingly.\n\n---\n\n# 22. Seller permissions\n\nThe publication markets available may eventually depend on:\n\n* account country;\n* individual/professional status;\n* verified identity;\n* KYC;\n* business verification;\n* professional subscription;\n* billing address;\n* VAT configuration;\n* category;\n* legal restrictions.\n\nCentralize these rules.\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\ncanSellerPublishInMarket({\n  seller,\n  market,\n  listing,\n});\n```\n\nDo not embed large permission expressions in React JSX.\n\n---\n\n# 23. Seller UX\n\nThe seller experience must remain simple even though the underlying model is powerful.\n\nPreferred publication UX:\n\n```text\n1. Cat\303\251gorie\n2. Description\n3. Photos\n4. Prix\n5. Livraison\n6. March\303\251s\n7. V\303\251rification\n8. Publication\n```\n\nAdapt this order to the current Shongre publication journey if necessary.\n\nDo not make the seller configure technical concepts such as currencies, locales or taxonomy IDs directly.\n\n---\n\n# 24. Professional sellers\n\nEnsure the feature works for both:\n\n```text\nParticulier\nProfessionnel\n```\n\nProfessional sellers may eventually need additional tools:\n\n* default publication markets;\n* bulk market assignment;\n* store markets;\n* catalog-wide markets;\n* market-specific inventory;\n* market-specific subscriptions.\n\nPrepare the architecture for these without overcomplicating the first implementation.\n\n---\n\n# 25. Default seller preferences\n\nAdd support for seller publication preferences such as:\n\n```ts\ndefaultPublicationMarketIds: string[];\n```\n\nFor example, a professional seller may choose:\n\n```text\nPublier par d\303\251faut dans :\n\342\234\223 France\n\342\234\223 Belgique\n```\n\nPublication should initialize from these preferences but allow editing when permitted.\n\n---\n\n# 26. Admin global market controls\n\nAdmin should be able to define:\n\n```text\nPlatform default market: France\n```\n\nand possibly:\n\n```text\nFallback market: France\n```\n\nNever hardcode `FR` throughout the application.\n\nExpose selectors/helpers such as:\n\n```ts\ngetDefaultMarket()\ngetActiveMarkets()\ngetMarketById()\ngetMarketsForCategory()\n```\n\n---\n\n# 27. Demo mode\n\nBecause Shongre currently has frontend/demo capabilities, implement deterministic fixtures demonstrating at least:\n\n### Markets\n\n```text\nFrance\nBelgique\nSuisse\nLuxembourg\n```\n\n### States\n\n* active market;\n* disabled market;\n* draft market;\n* category unavailable in market;\n* seller eligible in several markets;\n* seller eligible in one market only;\n* listing active in several markets;\n* listing with mixed per-market statuses.\n\nDo not create fake asynchronous APIs pretending a backend exists.\n\nUse the existing mock/demo data architecture.\n\n---\n\n# 28. Architecture\n\nAnalyze existing files first.\n\nDo not create another parallel market system if one already exists.\n\nPrefer a structure conceptually similar to:\n\n```text\nfrontend/\n  src/\n    domain/\n      markets/\n        types.ts\n        selectors.ts\n        permissions.ts\n        validation.ts\n\n    features/\n      markets/\n      publish/\n      admin/\n      search/\n\n    data/\n      markets/\n      marketTaxonomy/\n\n    components/\n      market/\n```\n\nAdapt names to the actual architecture.\n\nKeep:\n\n```text\nUI\n \342\206\223\nfeature/application layer\n \342\206\223\ndomain selectors/services\n \342\206\223\nrepository/data contracts\n```\n\nDo not let pages directly manipulate raw fixtures.\n\n---\n\n# 29. Backend-ready contracts\n\nAlthough this phase may primarily concern frontend implementation, ensure all models and operations can later map cleanly to APIs.\n\nPrepare repository interfaces/contracts such as:\n\n```ts\ninterface MarketRepository {\n  list(): Promise<Market[]>;\n  get(id: string): Promise<Market>;\n}\n\ninterface ListingMarketRepository {\n  getEligibleMarkets(input: EligibleMarketsInput): Promise<Market[]>;\n}\n```\n\nand eventual endpoints conceptually similar to:\n\n```text\nGET    /markets\nGET    /markets/:id\nGET    /markets/:id/taxonomy\n\nGET    /listings/:id/markets\n\nPOST   /listings/:id/markets\nPATCH  /listings/:id/markets/:marketId\nDELETE /listings/:id/markets/:marketId\n```\n\nFor admin:\n\n```text\nGET    /admin/markets\nPOST   /admin/markets\nPATCH  /admin/markets/:id\n\nGET    /admin/markets/:id/taxonomy\nPATCH  /admin/markets/:id/taxonomy\n```\n\nDo not implement fake network calls if no backend exists yet.\n\n---\n\n# 30. Search and indexing readiness\n\nEnsure the future search/indexing model can distinguish:\n\n```text\nlisting\n+\nmarket\n+\nmarket publication status\n```\n\nAn inactive market association must never make a listing visible in that market.\n\nA useful future indexing representation may resemble:\n\n```ts\n{\n  listingId: \"listing_123\",\n  activeMarketIds: [\"fr\", \"be\"],\n}\n```\n\nor one search document per `(listing, market)` if the search architecture eventually requires different localized data.\n\nKeep the current implementation flexible enough to support either.\n\n---\n\n# 31. Performance\n\nAvoid:\n\n* loading the entire global taxonomy repeatedly;\n* deep client-side scans on every render;\n* duplicating taxonomy trees per market;\n* expensive eligibility computations in JSX;\n* excessive localStorage access;\n* duplicate state between contexts/stores.\n\nUse:\n\n* normalized maps;\n* selectors;\n* memoization where useful;\n* existing state-management patterns.\n\n---\n\n# 32. Accessibility\n\nEnsure all multi-select controls are accessible.\n\nMarket selection must support:\n\n* keyboard navigation;\n* visible focus;\n* correct checkbox semantics;\n* screen-reader labels;\n* disabled-state explanation;\n* validation announcements;\n* no flag-only labels.\n\nNever rely solely on color or flags.\n\n---\n\n# 33. Responsive design\n\nEnsure the complete experience works on:\n\n* desktop web;\n* tablet;\n* mobile web;\n* iOS app/webview;\n* Android app/webview.\n\nOn mobile, market cards should become compact full-width rows.\n\nDo not allow horizontal overflow.\n\nAvoid oversized:\n\n* cards;\n* selectors;\n* modals;\n* text;\n* buttons;\n* spacing.\n\nUse existing responsive design tokens.\n\n---\n\n# 34. Design system\n\nUse existing Shongre primitives and tokens.\n\nDo not introduce:\n\n* hardcoded colors;\n* arbitrary radii;\n* duplicate buttons;\n* duplicate badges;\n* duplicate modal systems;\n* isolated spacing systems.\n\nReuse existing:\n\n* Button;\n* Badge;\n* FormField;\n* Modal/Drawer;\n* StatePanel;\n* Notice;\n* Checkbox;\n* SectionHeader;\n* admin table/list primitives;\n\nor their actual equivalents in the repository.\n\n---\n\n# 35. Admin UX quality\n\nAdmin market management should feel like a professional SaaS back office.\n\nUse:\n\n* clear information hierarchy;\n* compact controls;\n* search;\n* filters;\n* badges;\n* bulk actions;\n* confirmation dialogs;\n* impact previews;\n* empty states;\n* error states;\n* skeleton/loading states;\n* unsaved-changes indication where relevant.\n\nAvoid giant cards or unnecessarily large controls.\n\n---\n\n# 36. Market removal safety\n\nMarkets referenced by listings must not be physically deleted casually.\n\nPrefer:\n\n```text\ndisable\narchive\n```\n\ninstead of hard deletion.\n\nIf hard deletion exists, make it an exceptional protected operation.\n\n---\n\n# 37. Audit existing functionality\n\nBefore implementation, inspect all affected areas, including:\n\n```text\npublication flow\nlisting creation state\nlisting editing\nlisting management\nseller workspace\nseller store\nsearch\nresults\nhomepage\ntaxonomy\nfilters\nadmin\nmarket management\nmonetization\nauthentication\nseller roles\nlocalization\ncurrency\nrouting\ndemo fixtures\n```\n\nFind duplicated or inconsistent country/market concepts and consolidate them.\n\n---\n\n# 38. Migration and backward compatibility\n\nExisting listings that have no explicit market assignment must continue to work.\n\nIntroduce a migration/fallback rule such as:\n\n```text\nlegacy listing without market\n\342\206\222 default market = France\n```\n\nDo this in one centralized compatibility layer.\n\nDo not sprinkle:\n\n```ts\nmarketId ?? \"fr\"\n```\n\nthroughout the codebase.\n\n---\n\n# 39. Tests\n\nAdd/update tests covering at minimum:\n\n### Publication\n\n* France selected by default;\n* seller selects multiple markets;\n* seller deselects market;\n* disabled market cannot be selected;\n* unavailable category prevents selection;\n* market-specific validation;\n* successful multi-market publication.\n\n### Admin\n\n* create market;\n* enable/disable market;\n* configure category availability;\n* inherited taxonomy state;\n* override taxonomy state;\n* market disabled disappears from seller publication choices.\n\n### Listings\n\n* one listing available in several markets;\n* per-market status;\n* remove a market without deleting listing;\n* legacy listings resolve to France.\n\n### Search\n\n* listing appears only in active associated markets.\n\n### Roles\n\nTest at least:\n\n```text\nvisitor\nindividual seller\nprofessional seller\nadmin\nmoderator where relevant\n```\n\n---\n\n# 40. Acceptance criteria\n\nThe work is complete only when:\n\n* a seller can select **more than one market** during publication;\n* the listing remains one canonical listing;\n* each selected market has its own publication association/status;\n* France remains the default market;\n* markets come from centralized configuration;\n* admin can create/configure/enable/disable markets;\n* admin can associate categories with each market;\n* taxonomy is not unnecessarily duplicated;\n* publication options dynamically respect category/market compatibility;\n* seller receives clear feedback about unavailable markets;\n* market-specific validation works;\n* existing listings remain compatible;\n* seller workspace shows all markets for each listing;\n* seller can manage market availability after publication;\n* search visibility respects market assignment;\n* individual and professional sellers are supported;\n* demo mode contains realistic deterministic examples;\n* UI is polished, compact, responsive and accessible;\n* design tokens/primitives are respected;\n* no fake backend behavior is introduced;\n* domain contracts are ready for the future backend;\n* tests pass;\n* lint/typecheck/build pass.\n\n---\n\n# 41. Final verification\n\nAfter implementation:\n\n1. inspect every modified flow visually;\n2. test desktop, tablet and mobile;\n3. test Particulier publication;\n4. test Professionnel publication;\n5. test listing associated with one market;\n6. test listing associated with several markets;\n7. disable a category for one market and verify publication reacts immediately;\n8. disable an entire market and verify it disappears from eligible publication choices;\n9. verify an existing active listing is not accidentally deleted;\n10. verify search is market-aware;\n11. verify France remains the safe default for legacy data;\n12. run tests;\n13. run lint;\n14. run TypeScript checks;\n15. run production build;\n16. remove obsolete/duplicated implementation discovered during the migration.\n\nFinally, update `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or the appropriate architecture documentation with the resulting rules, especially the distinction between:\n\n```text\ncountry\nmarket\nbrowsing market\nlisting publication markets\ntaxonomy\nmarket taxonomy availability\n```\n\nThe resulting architecture must make adding a new country/market mostly a **configuration operation rather than a frontend code change**, while keeping the publication experience extremely simple for sellers."
    }
  }
}
